<title>USA: MEMC to invest $250 mln in wafer facilities.</title>
<headline>MEMC to invest $250 mln in wafer facilities.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERS, Mo. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>MEMC Electronic Materials Inc said Friday it has started to invest about $250 million to expand its 300mm (12 inch) wafer production capacity and speed development of that diameter wafer.</p>
<p>The silicon wafer maker said it has started construction on a 300mm integrated production facility adjacent to its existing plant in Utsunomiya, Japan, which should be ready for operations in mid-1998.</p>
<p>The facility in St. Peters, Mo., will provide additional crystal growing and wafer processing equipment, the company said in a press release.</p>
</text>
